# Data licence

The **code** in this repository is under the MIT licence — see [`LICENSE`](LICENSE).

The **measurements** are not code, and they are under a different licence, because
the point of this project is that other people reuse them:

> The contents of `data/` are licensed under the
> **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International** licence (CC BY 4.0).
> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>

## What that means in practice

**You may** copy, redistribute, remix, transform and build upon the data, for any
purpose, including commercially.

**You must** give appropriate credit: name LocBench, and link back to this
repository if you can. A sentence like *"data from LocBench
(github.com/…/locbench)"* is enough.

**No warranty.** The data is published as it came out of the machine, limits
included. Read [`PROTOCOL.md`](PROTOCOL.md), section 6, before drawing
conclusions from it. In particular: it is one machine, one GPU, one model
family, and two sessions.

## Why CC BY and not something stricter

Because a measurement nobody may reuse is a measurement nobody can check, and
being checkable is the entire claim. If a number here is wrong, the fastest way
to find out is for someone else to redo it.
